\]
which is divisible by $4$ and has at least $8$ divisors, contradicting
$\tau(n-2)\le4$. Hence this case is impossible for $n>24$.

Therefore $n-1$ must be prime. Since $n-1\neq 2$, it is odd, so $n-2$ is even.
The only even integers $\ge 23$ with at most $4$ divisors are of the form $2q$
with $q$ an odd prime. Thus
\[
n-2=2q,\qquad n-1=2q+1\ \text{prime}.
